shape theory.physics.su2 : theory.physics.gauge, theory.physics.u1 {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 3.4 (SU(2)-Complex).
// Any two generators projected as values give rotation mixing the
// two, producing SU(2). Three generator pairs produce three coupled
// SU(2) symmetries forming a spherical triangular structure on the
// unit sphere.
//
// SU(2)_XY, SU(2)_YZ, SU(2)_XZ
//
// The three pairs share legs: SU(2)_XY and SU(2)_YZ share Y, etc.
// The three vertices sit on the unit sphere, forming a spherical
// triangle preserving rotational symmetry.
//
// The SU(2)-complex is one coupled system, not three independent
// ones. Changing SU(2)_XY affects both SU(2)_XZ (through X)
// and SU(2)_YZ (through Y).
//
// Provides 3 internal dimensions: 2 circular motion + 1 rotational.
// Together with U(1)'s 3 translational: 6 total internal dimensions.
//
// Derives from: theory.physics.gauge, theory.physics.u1
  """
}
